      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "CONTEXT",
          "content": "Overweight and obesity rates have more than doubled among 12 to 17 year-olds over the past 25 years. To date, few studies have documented collaborative practices in activities aimed at promoting healthy eating and physical activity in schools, although collaboration is a key element in health promotion."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVES",
          "content": "To identify the determinants that influence collaborative practices in secondary schools. To define the role of the school nurse in these practices."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHOD",
          "content": "A descriptive multiple case study was conducted in three Quebec secondary schools. The methods used were: focus group; interviews (21); observation (5); and document review (3). Qualitative analysis was conducted by more than one researcher."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Determinants of collaborative practices relate to the individual, team and organization. The time needed to adapt to a role is a determinant that influences the contribution a newly appointed school nurse can make to collaborative practices in a school setting."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "Understanding the determinants that influence collaborative practices paves the way to establishing the conditions conducive to various stakeholders becoming involved in promoting the health of young people."
        }
      ]},
